      "q": "An electron is regarded as a universal particle. Explain.",
      "a": "The value of charge (e) and mass (m) of the electron always remain the same whatever may be the source of their emission. In the discharge tube, the electrons may be emitted either from the cathode or form the gas enclosed in the discharge tube. Whatever may be the metal which forms the cathode or the gas present in the discharge tube, these values remain the same. Therefore, electron is regarded as a universal particle."
